+   "h2": "What does a car battery test check?",
+   "html": "<p>A battery test measures the battery's condition: how much charge it holds and how much starting current it can still deliver. A good test also looks at the charging system, because a battery that keeps going flat is sometimes a charging fault, not a worn battery.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Battery condition:</strong> whether it can still hold charge and start the engine reliably.</li>\n<li><strong>Charging output:</strong> whether the alternator is charging the battery properly while the engine runs.</li>\n<li><strong>Stored faults:</strong> a scan can show battery or charging messages the car has logged.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Ask the technician to explain the result in plain words, so you know whether the battery is fine, weak or due for replacement.</p>"
