+   "h2": "When should you get your battery tested?",
+   "html": "<p>Do not wait for a car that will not start. These signs are worth a quick test:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The engine cranks more slowly than it used to, especially on a cold start after the car has sat.</li>\n<li>Start-stop stops working, or works less often than before.</li>\n<li>Battery or charging warning lights or messages appear on the dash.</li>\n<li>Headlights or interior lights dim at idle, or electrical features act up.</li>\n<li>The battery is several years old. Heat shortens battery life, and many last only a few years in Singapore.</li>\n<li>The car sits unused for weeks at a time.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>One of these signs does not prove the battery is the problem, which is why testing first beats guessing.</p>"
